  "verbalization": "Hydrocortisone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Allergic Rhinitis through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Hydrocortisone is linked to Acquired Angioedema, which in turn is associated with Alimemazine and Methdilazine, both of which are indicated to cause Allergic Rhinitis. This indicates a potential chain of interactions where Hydrocortisone may influence the development of allergic symptoms through the actions of these secondary compounds. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Hydrocortisone to Allergic Rhinitis highlights a possible role in the broader context of allergic inflammation, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these pathways suggests that Hydrocortisone may act as a precursor or modulator in the cascade leading to allergic rhinitis, though further research is needed to elucidate the precise relationship.",
